<title>INDIA: Indian soybean, meal steady, oil up.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean, meal steady, oil up.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady in central Indian markets on Wednesday, dealers said. Business volume was good and the undertone was steady. Soybean sowing was in full swing in central Indian areas.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were up by 100 rupees per tonne on limited selling at lower levels. Business volume was dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were steady in very limited trading. Soymeal yellow was $265-266 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) west coast Indian ports for export. Rapeseed extraction was $96-97 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export and was 3,250-3,300 rupees per tonne in FOR (free on rail) condition .</p>
